course: dictionary
lesson: 14128
title: The milligram
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A milligram is a very small unit of mass. Mass tells you how heavy something is. A milligram is one thousandth of a gram, so it weighs very little. A few grains of salt might weigh only a few milligrams.
explain: «The label on the bottle says 50 mg of vitamin C in each tablet.» Here mg is the short form of milligram. The label tells you how much of the vitamin is in one tablet, and the number is small because the amount is tiny.
explain: Remember the steps: 1000 milligrams make 1 gram, and 1000 grams make 1 kilogram. When you see «mg», think of a very light amount, and when you see «g» or «kg», think of something heavier.
fact: A milligram is one thousandth of a gram.
fact: 1000 milligrams = 1 gram, and 1000 grams = 1 kilogram.
fact: The short form (symbol) for milligram is «mg», with no full stop and no s.
fact: Medicine labels and food labels often give small amounts in milligrams.
exercise: «The tablet contains 200 mg of medicine.» What does mg stand for? | megabyte | millilitre | metre | *milligram
exercise: How many milligrams make 1 gram? | *1000 | 100 | 1 million | 10
exercise: Which of these weighs the least? | *1 milligram | 1 kilogram | 1 tonne | 1 gram
test: How many grams make 1000 milligrams? | 100 grams | 10 grams | *1 gram | 1 kilogram
test: Which is the correct short form of milligram? | ml | *mg | kg | g
exam: «A small bag holds 2 grams of sugar.» How many milligrams is that? | 20000 mg | *2000 mg | 20 mg | 200 mg
